---
// The story is the founder's own, approved on 2026-10-12. No personal details are shown.
import { appUrl, shopUrl } from "../config";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Why HisFullGlory exists, what we are building, and how we handle Scripture, context, privacy and the community."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>About HisFullGlory</h1>
      <p class="lede">A calm place to come back to Scripture, each day.</p>

      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        HisFullGlory began with something I noticed in my own life: how easily
        faith slips into the background when the days get full. It never
        happened through one big decision. It was one busy week after another.
      </p>
      <p>
        I wanted to build something that makes it a little easier to come back.
        Back to Scripture, to prayer, and to a few honest minutes of reflection,
        again each day.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are building</h2>
      <p>HisFullGlory is meant to be more than a shop.</p>
      <p>
        The HisFullGlory app is the heart of it: Scripture for today, a private
        journal, prayer and a community to talk things through. It is a beta web
        app, so it opens in your browser and is still growing.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website is where you can read the whole Bible, with context notes
        that name their sources. More is being added step by step.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both link to our shop, where you will find a small selection of study
        Bibles, chosen with care.
      </p>

      <h2>What I hope for</h2>
      <p>
        I cannot make anyone’s faith grow, and neither can a website or an app.
        That is God’s work. What I can do is build something calm and honest
        that keeps pointing back to His Word and gently encourages a daily walk
        with God.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our motto is Jesus at the Center. It is also the test for everything we
        add.
      </p>

      <h2>How we handle Scripture and context</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Scripture comes first. We use the World English Bible, a public-domain
          translation.
        </li>
        <li>
          Context notes name their sources. A note that has not yet been
          reviewed by a theological reader is labelled “Editorial draft”.
        </li>
        <li>
          Community voices are labelled as community. Popularity does not make
          something true.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy and care in the community</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your journal and private prayers stay on your own device unless you
          choose to share something.
        </li>
        <li>
          Before posting, you agree to the community rules. You can report,
          block or mute, and you can post anonymously.
        </li>
        <li>There are no ads in the community.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a question or an idea, we would love to hear it.
        <a href={`${shopUrl}/pages/contact`}>Contact us</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={appUrl}>Open the app</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/bible">Explore the Bible</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 8px;
  }
  ul {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
